; A declaration template generating a form outside the template
; surface - refused AT THE MACRO'S OWN LINE, before any invocation
; exists: the loud-at-definition shape, and the reachable producer
; AX3021 was promised when its default-arm-refuses rule was written
; (macro-system.md MAC-CAP-2 - "the ninth form refuses in the commit
; that adds it").
;
; This fixture has now been overtaken TWICE by the surface it guards:
; it used a `data` template until 2026-08-15, when `data` and `struct`
; became template kinds, and then a `type` alias until later the same
; day, when `type` and `effect` did. Each time it stopped producing a
; diagnostic at all - a golden going silent because the language grew
; under it, which the JSON derivation caught both times rather than
; the eye.
;
; A nested `macro` is the refusal now, and it is a refusal by DECISION
; rather than by schedule, which is what makes it a stable subject: a
; macro generated in phase D would have to join the macro table the
; same fixpoint is reading. (`trait` was tried here first and does not
; reach AX3021 at all - a trait declaration inside a template is
; AX2003 at the parser, which is a different fact about a different
; layer.)
(macro defAlias ((defAlias nm)
   (macro (nm x) x)))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
